lds with at least one resident child aged 0–17 years\"}]}, {\"v\": \"before/after or trend\", \"ev\": [{\"loc\": \"summary\", \"q\": \"The number of persons with active epilepsy increased compared with earlier years, likely because of population growth.\"}]}, {\"v\": \"surveillance/descriptive\", \"ev\": [{\"loc\": \"summary\", \"q\": \"This study provides updated national estimates and the first modeled estimates of active epilepsy cases for all States.\"}]}], \"methods_quotes\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"yielded state-level estimates of active epilepsy, indirectly standardized for age and income\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"as the variance of the product of these two random variables yielded 95% confidence intervals\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"NHIS and NSCH data was used to calculate the prevalence (proportion) of active epilepsy for three age groups\"}, {\"loc\": \"note\", \"q\": \"Confidence interval represents only sampling uncertainty\"}], \"confidence\": \"medium\", \"uncertain_fields\": [\"study_design\"]}", "type": "text"}]}